{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Tile tuning shows 512 packed words is consistently better than the current 2048-word tile. I’m also testing a two-pass boundary strategy: the streaming pass writes only all-zero/all-one words, and a tiny rowwise pass repairs the single mixed word per row. This removes a variable 64-bit shift from nearly every output word."}}
